<title>UK: ICI down on broker downgrades.</title>
<headline>ICI down on broker downgrades.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Chemical Industries Plc eased 10p to 738 by 0926 on Monday after brokerage Dresdner Kleinwort Benson downgraded the stock, dealers said.  </p>
<p>The broker's analyst Jeremy Chantry said he cut his rating on the stock to &quot;sell&quot; from &quot;hold&quot; and trimmed his 1997 and 1998 earnings per share estimates to 46p from 51p and to 55p from 61p, respectively.</p>
<p>The downgrades reflect &quot;an underlying difficult trading environment,&quot; the analyst said.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
